istration<T> getBeanRegistration(BeanDefinition<? extends T> definition, Argument<T> type,","+                                                BeanResolutionContext.Segment<?, ?> lookupPoint);","+","     /**","      * Destroys and forgets a registration this resolver owns, before its owner is destroyed. A shared registration","      * is never destroyed. Registration identity, rather than equality of bean definitions or instances, identifies"],"additions":26,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"inject/src/main/java/io/micronaut/context/BeanResolutionContext.java","lines":["@@ -173,6 +173,28 @@ default <R> R withDependencies(Function<BeanDependencyGroup, R> action) {","      */","     <T> BeanRegistration<T> getBeanRegistration(BeanDefinition<? extends T> definition, Argument<T> beanType);"," ","+    /**","+     * Resolves the registration of the bean of the given definition as the given bean type at the given point, on","+     * behalf of the bean this context resolves for.","+     *","+     * <p>This is {@link #getBeanRegistration(BeanDefinition, Argument)} with the lookup point pushed onto the path","+     * for the resolution: a bean the resolution creates sees the lookup point as the point it is created for, as an","+     * injected {@link io.micronaut.inject.InjectionPoint} does, and the dependency graph records the bean this","+     * context resolves for as receiving it there. The path is as it was once the resolution returns.</p>","+     *","+     * @param definition  The bean definition","+     * @param beanType    The potentially parameterized bean type to resolve the definition as","+     * @param lookupPoint The segment the resolution is made at, whose declaring type is the definition of the bean","+     *                    this context resolves for, or a segment that narrows one of the path","+     * @param <T>         The bean type","+     * @return The bean registration","+     * @throws io.micronaut.context.exceptions.NoSuchBeanException if the 